STAGED PATCH 0003 of 5: apply after 0005.
Target: Linux 6.12.116, mm/vmalloc.c. Line anchors are the
patch-point list's numbers of record; context lines are
schematic. Re-base on the real tree before applying.

Subject: iscandar: vmalloc backing at 2.3, free door at 2.4

The family splits at its own seam (reconciliation, Family
2): the reservation half (2.2, __get_vm_area_node and
alloc_vmap_area) stays stock, address-space bookkeeping
that was never part of the replacement, and is not patched.
Only the backing is replaced: where the stock body fills
the area's page array page by page from the page allocator,
the bridge serves ONE exact-fit run for the whole area, at
the standing calibration of one sector to one page, and
the array is filled with the run's frames in order.

One vmalloc contains a hidden slab allocation (the
page-pointer array, allocated by a recursive vmalloc call
into Family 1, per the patch list): it arrives at 1.1 as
any cache allocation does, and the layer's books expect
vmalloc traffic to touch Family 1 in this way.

The frame binding: area->pages[] takes struct page
pointers, which the glue forms from the arena's reserved
physical range (iscandar_offset_to_page, 0005). That range
is why the arena in the live system is a reserved physical
span and not an anonymous mapping: the bench binding step
is carried in BUILD-STATUS.md.

--- a/mm/vmalloc.c
+++ b/mm/vmalloc.c
@@ -3594,7 +3594,30 @@
-static int vm_area_alloc_pages(...)
+static int vm_area_alloc_pages(...)
 {
+	if (iscandar_active()) {
+		struct IscandarBridgeRecord rec = { };
+		unsigned int i;
+
+		rec.op = ISCANDAR_OP_VMALLOC_BACKING;
+		rec.size = (u64)area->nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT;
+		if (iscandar_bridge_call(&rec)
+		    || rec.status != ISCANDAR_BRIDGE_OK)
+			return -ENOMEM;
+		for (i = 0; i < area->nr_pages; i++)
+			area->pages[i] =
+				iscandar_offset_to_page(rec.result) + i;
+		return 0;
+	}
+	iscandar_prefix_note(ISCANDAR_CENTER_VMALLOC_BACKING,
+			     (size_t)area->nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT);
 	...
 }
@@ -3407,6 +3430,18 @@
-void vfree(const void *addr)
+void vfree(const void *addr)
 {
+	if (iscandar_ptr_in_arena(addr)) {
+		struct IscandarBridgeRecord rec = { };
+
+		rec.op = ISCANDAR_OP_VFREE;
+		rec.size = iscandar_ptr_to_offset(addr);
+		(void)iscandar_bridge_call(&rec);
+		return;
+	}
 	...
 }
@@ -3373,4 +3408,8 @@
-void vfree_atomic(const void *addr)
+void vfree_atomic(const void *addr)
 {
+	/* Same door as vfree: the bridge free path does not
+	 * sleep in this build's serving arrangement (the call
+	 * completes synchronously), so the atomic door takes
+	 * the same range decision and the same record. If the
+	 * bench build makes the call blocking, this door is
+	 * where that finding lands; it is not pre-decided. */
 	...
 }
